      <h1>Meta + Google Performance Ads for Dermatology + Skin Clinics — India + GCC + International 2026 Playbook</h1>
      <p class="lede">How to run Meta + Google ads for a clinic profitably in Dermatology + Skin Clinics? This guide covers costs, tactics, tools, timelines, compliance, and real outcomes from ITD GrowthLabs&#x27; work across 20+ clinic engagements in India + GCC. We currently manage full-stack digital marketing for a premium dermatology brand with 5+ clinics across India (client name shared under NDA). Serves all major India cities (Mumbai + Delhi + Bangalore + Ahmedabad + Hyderabad + Chennai + Pune + Kolkata + Gurgaon + Noida + Jaipur + Chandigarh + Thane + Navi Mumbai + Nashik + Nagpur + Lucknow + Indore + Kochi + Coimbatore), GCC (Dubai + Abu Dhabi + Sharjah + Riyadh + Jeddah + Doha + Kuwait City + Manama + Muscat), and international markets (London + Singapore + more).</p>
      <a class="book-cta" href="/industries/digital-marketing-for-doctors.php#packages">See Packages + Book Free Growth Audit &rarr;</a>
      <div class="cities">Serving India + GCC + International: Mumbai · Delhi · Bangalore · Ahmedabad · Hyderabad · Chennai · Pune · Kolkata · Gurgaon · Noida · Jaipur · Chandigarh · Lucknow · Indore + more</div>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <div class="doc-container narrow">
        <h2>12 Answers Doctors Ask Us About Meta + Google Performance Ads</h2>
        <p class="lede">Analysis based on ITD GrowthLabs' work across 20+ clinic engagements in India + GCC. Client names + case study details shared on discovery call under NDA.</p>

          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How much should a dermatology clinic spend on Meta + Google ads?</h3>
            <div>Realistic ad-spend ranges for dermatology and skin clinics in Mumbai: Starter/solo doctor Rs 30-80K/month. Growth 2-3 doctor clinic Rs 80K-2 lakh/month. Premium multi-location or premium single-clinic Rs 2-6 lakh/month. Enterprise chains + hospitals Rs 6-25 lakh/month. Split: 50-60% Meta (Instagram + Facebook + Reels ads), 30-40% Google (Search + YouTube + Performance Max), 5-10% experimental (Snapchat if premium GCC audience). ITD passes ad spend through at zero markup.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What&#x27;s a reasonable cost per patient inquiry for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>Cost per qualified inquiry varies by AOV. Low-AOV visits (dental cleaning, dermatology consult, pediatrics): Rs 150-500/inquiry. Mid-AOV (skin treatments, orthodontics, ENT procedures): Rs 500-1,500/inquiry. High-AOV (IVF, cosmetic surgery, cardiac procedures, hair transplant): Rs 1,500-8,000/inquiry. What matters is inquiry-to-booking conversion + LTV, not just CPI.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Which Meta ad format works best for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>Ranked by ROAS for Dermatology + Skin Clinics: (1) Reels ads on top-performing organic Reels — 2-4x other formats, (2) Advantage+ Creative + Audience with best 30 asset combinations, (3) Click-to-WhatsApp (CTWA) direct-response ads, (4) Meta Lead Ads with instant forms, (5) carousel ads for procedure explainers. Avoid: static single-image ads (worst CTR), boosted posts (worst ROAS).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Should a dermatology clinic run Google ads?</h3>
            <div>Yes, particularly Search + Performance Max. High-intent searches (dermatologist, skin clinic, acne, pigmentation, laser, HydraFacial, Botox, fillers + city) convert 2-4x better than social discovery. Best-performing Google campaigns for dermatology and skin clinics: (1) exact-match branded terms — highest ROAS, (2) specialty-keyword Search ads — bulk of new patient acquisition, (3) YouTube Bumper + Skippable for awareness in premium AOV specialties, (4) Performance Max for retargeting + Gmail + Discovery.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does WhatsApp CTWA ads work for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>Click-to-WhatsApp Meta ads open a pre-filled WhatsApp conversation directly to your clinic. Best practice for Dermatology + Skin Clinics: (1) Reel or carousel ad with strong hook (e.g., 'Curious about [specific procedure]? Chat with our team on WhatsApp'), (2) pre-filled message like 'Hi, I'd like to know more about [procedure]', (3) WhatsApp Cloud API auto-responder qualifies patient in 3-5 questions, (4) inside-sales handles high-AOV escalation, (5) booking closed via calendar link. Typical CTWA cost per qualified conversation Rs 150-800.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does ITD handle Meta CAPI + Google Enhanced Conversions for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>Full server-side attribution: (1) Meta Conversion API via GTM + Zapier for offline patient bookings + procedures, (2) Google Enhanced Conversions with hashed email + phone + first-party data, (3) LTV-based bidding by patient specialty + AOV cohort, (4) call tracking with dynamic phone-number swap, (5) offline conversion upload for closed procedures. Attribution accuracy improves from ~40% (client-side) to 85-95% (server-side).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>What ad creatives convert best for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>Top ad creative patterns for Dermatology + Skin Clinics: (1) doctor-on-camera hook + credential + procedure explainer (5-15 sec), (2) 3-second problem statement + solution reveal, (3) real patient testimonial (with consent) — often highest CTR, (4) UGC-style before-after (compliance-safe), (5) 'What most patients don't know about dermatology...' myth-busting hook. ITD produces 15-40 creative variants/month for velocity + fatigue avoidance.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How long before Meta + Google ads become profitable for a dermatology clinic?</h3>
            <div>Typical Meta + Google ads maturity curve for dermatology and skin clinics: Week 1-2 = learning phase (elevated CPI). Week 3-6 = first stable ROAS baselines. Month 2-3 = optimization + creative iteration (ROAS improves 30-60%). Month 4-6 = compounding retargeting + LAL audiences (ROAS improves further 20-40%). Month 6+ = predictable inquiry pipeline. Break-even usually month 2-3, ROI positive month 4+.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Should we run ads during festivals + monsoon in Mumbai?</h3>
            <div>Seasonality tips for Dermatology + Skin Clinics in Mumbai: (1) monsoon = boost skin + hair + respiratory + dental (higher patient concern), (2) wedding season Sep-Feb = boost dermatology + cosmetic + dental, (3) new-year resolution Jan-Feb = fitness + orthopedics + weight loss, (4) academic break May-June = pediatrics + orthodontics. Ad-spend up-weight 20-40% in your specialty's peak season.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does ITD prevent ad fatigue for dermatology?</h3>
            <div>Ad fatigue defense stack: (1) 15-40 creative variants/month for continuous refresh, (2) audience rotation (LAL 1% / 2% / 5% / broad Advantage+ / retargeting), (3) creative-level frequency capping (max 3 impressions/user/7 days per creative), (4) fresh Reels ads weekly from top-performing organics, (5) offer + hook rotation, (6) A/B test velocity 3-8/week. Ad fatigue is the #1 killer of ROAS at scale.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>How does ITD report Meta + Google ads performance to a dermatology clinic?</h3>
            <div>Weekly: spend + patient inquiries + CPI + booking + ROAS by campaign + creative + audience. Monthly QBR: full P&L attribution + LTV cohorts + creative winners + audience insights + next-month plan. Quarterly: cohort revenue attribution + LTV/CAC + strategic roadmap. Live dashboard (Google Data Studio) shared with clinic team. Meta + Google account access remains 100% with clinic (we admin-user).</div>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-faq-item">
            <h3>Can ITD run ads for multi-location dermatology clinics?</h3>
            <div>Yes — Premium tier for 2-5 locations, Enterprise for 5-30+ locations. Multi-location strategy: (1) separate Meta + Google campaigns per location for radius targeting, (2) location-specific creative with local landmarks + city names, (3) per-location Google Business Profile ads (Local Service Ads for specialty-qualified verticals), (4) per-location call tracking + WhatsApp routing, (5) centralized attribution + per-location performance reporting.</div>
          </div>
      </div>
